  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 317 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nWe could see another opportunity for storms over the weekend as the \nupper-level trough in the Pacific Northwest tries to push into our \narea but it will be fighting the upper-level ridge over the SE US. A \nsurface low over the Central Plains will bring another cold front to \nour area but with the battle between the upper-level trough and \nridge, that front will potentially stall out over our forecast area \nbringing the potential for multiple rounds of rain Saturday and \nSunday night. The ridge begins to flatten out early next week and \nthere is high confidence the cold front will move off to the SE on \nMonday with the 25th to 75th percentile ensemble spread indicating \nhigh temperatures in the 70s.",
